sues/113681","id":3796411193,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iSKM5","user":{"login":"lostminds","id":17763524,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYzNTI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17763524?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds","html_url":"https://github.com/lostminds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lostminds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-25T10:35:57Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T10:35:57Z","body":"> Anyone know a workaround?\n\nThis last example at least looks like https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99715 the issue that viewport texture colors use premultiplied alpha. So to get such textures to render correctly with transparency you need to use a CanvasItem material set to use premultiplied alpha. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3796411193/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3797147389","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113681#issuecomment-3797147389","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113681","id":3797147389,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iU979","user":{"login":"h0lley","id":23386940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzg2OTQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23386940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/h0lley","html_url":"https://github.com/h0lley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h0lley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h0lley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h0lley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h0lley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h0lley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h0lley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h0lley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h0lley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h0lley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-25T19:48:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T19:49:09Z","body":"@lostminds that doesn't seem to help in the case of this issue.\n\nhere are the various setups taken with v4.6.rc2.official [78c6632eb] (in the context of this issue most importantly the last two ones):\n\nProject settings rendering/viewport/hdr_2d = false\nSubViewport use_hdr_2d = false\nTextureRect (ViewportTexutre) material = none\n\n<img width=\"932\" height=\"521\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9a62dbfc-f54d-4d10-9bad-f4994f02d1df\" />\n\nProject settings rendering/viewport/hdr_2d = false\nSubViewport use_hdr_2d = false\nTextureRect (ViewportTexutre) material = CanvasItemMaterial with premultiplied alpha\n\n<img width=\"934\" height=\"526\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1966ce44-9e4d-4483-bcca-e4ee28b8bdee\" />\n\nProject settings rendering/viewport/hdr_2d = true\nSubViewport use_hdr_2d = false\nTextureRect (ViewportTexutre) material = none\n\n<img width=\"855\" height=\"476\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8a360a8-799a-4382-b87c-8d99f286d276\" />\n\nProject settings rendering/viewport/hdr_2d = true\nSubViewport use_hdr_2d = false\nTextureRect (ViewportTexutre) material = CanvasItemMaterial with premultiplied alpha\n\n<img width=\"847\" height=\"472\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9e94e60c-dfc6-4ea7-b256-03b694e9051f\" />\n\nProject settings rendering/viewport/hdr_2d = false\nSubViewport use_hdr_2d = true\nTextureRect (ViewportTexutre) material = none\n\n<img width=\"857\" height=\"487\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/37fd21f1-7d0b-4f8c-95c6-da9d2f5ffb83\" />\n\nProject settings rendering/viewport/hdr_2d = false\nSubViewport use_hdr_2d = true\nTextureRect (ViewportTexutre) material = CanvasItemMaterial with premultiplied alpha\n\n<img width=\"857\" height=\"479\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2f93913-4736-41c5-a346-545608545c3e\" />\n\nProject settings rendering/viewport/hdr_2d = true\nSubViewport use_hdr_2d = true\nTextureRect (ViewportTexutre) material = none\n\n<img width=\"851\" height=\"478\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bc56c043-571e-42b3-a01c-fd0556d04eb2\" />\n\nProject settings rendering/viewport/hdr_2d = true\nSubViewport use_hdr_2d = true\nTextureRect (ViewportTexutre) material = CanvasItemMaterial with premultiplied alpha\n\n<img width=\"853\" height=\"473\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2edcedef-58af-42eb-a7ae-7ed0414b3f8c\" />\n\nthere doesn't seem to be a setup where we can enable use_hdr_2d on the SubViewport and still get expected additive blending.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3797147389/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3819967205","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113681#issuecomment-3819967205","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113681","id":3819967205,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jsBLl","user":{"login":"ultigonio","id":59210738,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MjEwNzM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59210738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio","html_url":"https://github.com/ultigonio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ultigonio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T19:56:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T20:05:15Z","body":"> This last example at least looks like [#99715](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99715) the issue that viewport texture colors use premultiplied alpha. So to get such textures to render correctly with transparency you need to use a CanvasItem material set to use premultiplied alpha.\n\nAs far as I can tell, this will work well enough when additive materials are being used with e.g. white particles that have transparent backgrounds. However, it will do absolutely nothing to cases where one tries to make a sprite with additive material black in order to make it transparent, or cases where particles have black backgrounds (which most particles from pre-made particle packs do). I'm bumping up against this issue as well and it's seeming like I may just need to take the L and remove almost all of the additively-blended particles I've made for my game so far, or replace them with particles that don't have black/dark patches.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3819967205/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]